JavaScript Internship

About This Repository

This repository contains my JavaScript internship assignments and capstone mini project. It demonstrates my learning and practical implementation of core JavaScript concepts.

Assignments

Assignment 1: Variables, Data Types, and Console Operations

- Variables using "var", "let", and "const"
- JavaScript data types
- Console output and "typeof"

Assignment 2: Operators, Expressions, and Input Handling

- Arithmetic and assignment operators
- User input using "prompt()"
- Type conversion using "Number()"
- Tip calculator

Assignment 3: Conditional Logic Implementation

- "if...else" statements
- "switch" statements
- Ternary operator
- Grade and pass/fail evaluation

Assignment 4: Loop Control Structures

- "for", "while", and "do...while" loops
- "break" and "continue"
- Multiplication table and number searching

Assignment 5: Function Architecture and Scope

- Standard and arrow functions
- Default parameters
- Function scope and block scope

Assignment 6: Arrays, Objects, and Core Methods

- Arrays of objects
- "forEach()", "filter()", and "map()"
- Product filtering and formatted reports

Capstone Mini Project

Project Title: Interactive Product Inventory & Analytics Dashboard

The project combines JavaScript concepts in a product inventory application.

Features

- Accepts product details using "prompt()"
- Validates product names and prices
- Assigns Budget, Standard, and Premium categories
- Calculates total inventory value
- Demonstrates tax and discount calculations
- Filters affordable products
- Generates formatted product reports

Technologies Used

- HTML
- JavaScript
- Visual Studio Code
- Node.js
- GitHub

How to Run

- Run JavaScript assignment files using Node.js in the terminal.
- Open the mini project's "index.html" file in a web browser.
- Enter product details when prompted and open the browser console to view the analytics.

Learning Outcomes

Through these assignments and the mini project, I practiced JavaScript variables, data types, operators, conditions, loops, functions, scope, arrays, objects, and array methods.

